NotesFinder – OCR Application

Project Overview

NotesFinder is a web-based OCR (Optical Character Recognition) application developed using Python and Streamlit. The application allows users to upload an image containing text and automatically extract the text from the image.

The project is designed to make it easier to convert handwritten or printed notes available in image format into editable digital text.

Objectives

- To extract text from images using OCR technology.
- To provide a simple and user-friendly web interface.
- To reduce the need for manual typing of text from images.
- To convert image-based notes into editable digital text.
- To provide a lightweight and accessible OCR solution.

Features

- Upload images through a web interface.
- Extract text automatically from uploaded images.
- Display the extracted text clearly.
- Simple and easy-to-use Streamlit interface.
- Supports common image formats.
- Can be deployed as a web application.

Technologies Used

Technology| Purpose
Python| Application development
Streamlit| Web interface
OpenCV| Image processing
OCR| Text extraction
NumPy| Image and data processing

Project Structure

NotesFinder/
│
├── app.py
├── ocr_utils.py
├── requirements.txt
├── README.md
└── sample/
    └── sample_image.jpg

File Description

- "app.py" – Main Streamlit application.
- "ocr_utils.py" – Contains the OCR-related functions used for text extraction.
- "requirements.txt" – Contains the required Python libraries.
- "README.md" – Project documentation.
- "sample/" – Contains sample images for testing the application.

Installation

1. Clone the Repository

2. Navigate to the Project Folder

cd NotesFinder

3. Install Required Dependencies

pip install -r requirements.txt

Running the Application

Start the Streamlit application using:

streamlit run app.py

The application will open in your web browser.

How to Use

1. Open the NotesFinder application.
2. Upload an image containing text.
3. The application processes the uploaded image.
4. OCR extracts the text from the image.
5. The extracted text is displayed on the screen.
6. The user can copy the extracted text for further use.

Application Workflow

User
  |
  v
Upload Image
  |
  v
Image Processing
  |
  v
OCR Text Extraction
  |
  v
Extracted Text
  |
  v
Display in Streamlit

Requirements

Make sure the following are installed:

- Python 3.x
- pip
- Required Python packages listed in "requirements.txt"

Install all dependencies using:

pip install -r requirements.txt

Deployment

The application can be deployed using cloud platforms such as Render.

The repository should contain the following files:

app.py
ocr_utils.py
requirements.txt
README.md

The deployment platform installs the required dependencies from "requirements.txt" and runs the Streamlit application.

Future Enhancements

The project can be further improved by adding:

- Support for multiple image uploads.
- Download extracted text as a ".txt" file.
- PDF document support.
- Improved handwritten text recognition.
- Text editing functionality.
- Search functionality for extracted notes.
- Support for multiple languages.
- Improved image preprocessing for better OCR accuracy.

Advantages

- Simple and user-friendly interface.
- Reduces manual typing.
- Fast text extraction from images.
- Easy to deploy.
- Useful for digitizing study notes and documents.
- Can be extended with additional OCR features.

Use Cases

NotesFinder can be useful for:

- Digitizing handwritten or printed study notes.
- Extracting text from educational materials.
- Converting image-based documents into editable text.
- Quickly copying text from photographs of notes.
- Creating digital versions of physical documents.

